{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler stitch task (#5428) to implement srd065-factor requirements R3.1-R3.4 in the go-unix-utils project. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.1: When --help is the first argument, print usage message to stdout and exit 0\n   - R3.2: When --version is the first argument, print version info to stdout and exit 0\n   - R3.3: Write factorization output to stdout, one line per integer\n   - R3.4: Write error messages to stderr without stopping processing of remaining inputs\n   \n   The task requires modifying `cmd/factor/main.go` and `cmd/factor/factor_test.go`, then verifying with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against `gfactor` (Homebrew GNU reference)\n   - SIGPIPE handler (`sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`) required at start of main\n   - Reference binary lookup with `exec.LookPath(\"gfactor\")` and `t.Skip` if not found\n   - Binary name normalization in tests using regex to handle path differences between Go and reference binaries\n   - Trial division factorization algorithm for int64 range\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd065-factor.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining all requirements for factor. R3 group has 4 items (R3.1-R3.4) covering help, version, stdout output, and stderr error handling.\n     - Non-goals: no arbitrary-precision beyond int64, no advanced factorization algorithms.\n\n   - `cmd/factor/main.go` (existing, to be modified)\n     - Already has --help and --version handling in main() (lines 29-38)\n     - Already writes factorization to stdout via `fmt.Println` in `printFactors`\n     - Already writes errors to stderr via `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` in `processArgs` and `processStdin`\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // factor prints the prime factorization of each integer.\n     //\n     // Specification: srd065-factor R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"math\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: factor [NUMBER]...\n     Print the prime factors of each specified integer.\n     `\n     const versionText = `factor (go-unix-utils) 0.1.0`\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             switch os.Args[1] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Print(helpText)\n                 return\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Println(versionText)\n                 return\n             }\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             exitCode = processArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         } else {\n             exitCode = processStdin()\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     \n     func processArgs(args []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if err := factorize(arg); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"factor: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func processStdin() int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         scanner := bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)\n         for scanner.Scan() {\n             line := strings.TrimSpace(scanner.Text())\n             if line == \"\" { continue }\n             if err := factorize(line); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"factor: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func factorize(input string) error {\n         n, err := strconv.ParseInt(input, 10, 64)\n         if err != nil { return fmt.Errorf(\"'%s' is not a valid positive integer\", input) }\n         if n < 0 { return fmt.Errorf(\"'%s' is not a valid positive integer\", input) }\n         factors := primeFactors(n)\n         printFactors(n, factors)\n         return nil\n     }\n     \n     func primeFactors(n int64) []int64 {\n         if n <= 1 { return nil }\n         var factors []int64\n         for n%2 == 0 { factors = append(factors, 2); n /= 2 }\n         limit := int64(math.Sqrt(float64(n)))\n         for d := int64(3); d <= limit; d += 2 {\n             for n%d == 0 { factors = append(factors, d); n /= d }\n             limit = int64(math.Sqrt(float64(n)))\n         }\n         if n > 1 { factors = append(factors, n) }\n         return factors\n     }\n     \n     func printFactors(n int64, factors []int64) {\n         var b strings.Builder\n         fmt.Fprintf(&b, \"%d:\", n)\n         for _, f := range factors { fmt.Fprintf(&b, \" %d\", f) }\n         fmt.Println(b.String())\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` (existing, to be modified)\n     - Has 16 differential test cases covering R1-R2 requirements\n     - Uses `normalizeBinaryName` regex to normalize binary name differences in error messages\n     - Missing test cases for --help and --version flags (R3.1, R3.2)\n     - Full existing test code included above in file read output\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted before implementation began.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed existing code against R3.1-R3.4 requirements. Found that the existing implementation already handles all four R3.x requirements functionally (--help, --version, stdout output, stderr errors with continuation). The main work needed is:\n     1. Update the package doc comment to include R3.1-R3.4 in the specification reference\n     2. Add differential test cases for --help and --version flags\n     3. Potentially verify existing behavior matches gfactor exactly for help/version output\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive user message containing the full stitch task description with: role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. The task is \"[stitch] cmd/factor: srd065 R3.1-R3.4\".\n   - Second user message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/factor/main.go`: Update spec comment to reference R3.1-R3.4 (the functional code already exists)\n   - Modify `cmd/factor/factor_test.go`: Add test cases for --help and --version flags\n   - Run `go build -o bin/factor ./cmd/factor/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/factor/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/factor/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, factor_test.go) and was about to begin implementation. The key insight from the reading is that the existing `cmd/factor/main.go` already implements R3.1-R3.4 functionally:\n   - R3.1 (--help): handled at lines 30-32\n   - R3.2 (--version): handled at lines 33-35  \n   - R3.3 (stdout): `printFactors` uses `fmt.Println` which writes to stdout\n   - R3.4 (stderr + continue): `processArgs` and `processStdin` write to stderr and continue loop\n   \n   The remaining work is primarily:\n   1. Update the package doc comment from `R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4` to include `R3.1-R3.4`\n   2. Add differential test cases for `--help` and `--version` to the test file\n   3. Build and test\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Modify `cmd/factor/main.go` to update the specification comment to include R3.1-R3.4, then modify `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` to add differential test cases for --help and --version flags (R3.1, R3.2). The --help/--version tests will need the `normalizeBinaryName` normalizer since output will contain the binary name. Then run build, vet, and test to verify acceptance criteria AC1-AC5.\n   \n   The task description states: \"Extend factor implementation for srd065 R3.1-R3.4\" and \"Add differential test cases covering R3.1-R3.4\". The acceptance criteria require: \"All R3.1-R3.4 requirements from srd065-factor.yaml are implemented in cmd/factor/main.go\" (AC1), \"Differential test cases added to cmd/factor/factor_test.go for each R3.x requirement\" (AC2), build succeeds (AC3), vet passes (AC4), and tests pass (AC5).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5428/8154b1e0-ed8f-4bba-876a-8feaa333f5c9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8154b1e0-ed8f-4bba-876a-8feaa333f5c9","uuid":"89eb80c8-7218-4b2d-ae8c-bd214314ec53","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:57:57.796Z","isSynthetic":true}
